/// at all -- faster, and constant-time where LLVM's carries were not.
/// Generated by `gen_asm_mul.py`; held to the Rust CIOS by the tests and,
/// on the chip, by the probe.
///
/// Never inlined: the body is about a thousand instructions with thirteen
/// registers pinned, and a point doubling has thirteen multiplies. Inlined,
/// those copies outgrow the instruction cache and every multiply runs from
/// flash -- the first build was seven times slower than the Rust (round 3).
